From a82efacb08348ff25851aaa63cceaf4d760c4a12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kumar Ankit <186563577+krank-09@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:52:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat: build role-based dashboards

T06: visible loading, error and live-connection states across the
Admin, Bob and Charlie dashboards.

Shared (common.js, components.css)
- notify(): non-blocking toasts replace alert() and silent failures
- setBusy(): consistent busy state for action buttons
- api(): network failure reports "server unreachable" instead of "Failed to fetch"
- WebSocket reconnect uses capped exponential backoff (1 s to 15 s); a
  "live updates paused" bar marks data as possibly stale while offline
- a render error in one live event shows a warning instead of breaking the feed

Bob / Charlie (verifier.js, bob.js)
- empty state shows "Connecting..." until the first init_sync
- forgery forward: success, quarantine-refused (423) and error toasts
- guard against a transmission without a threat_report

Admin (admin.js, routing-page.js)
- a threat card is only left armed if the server confirms; failures roll back
- refused (423) and failed sends, chain check, history and incidents
  failures are shown, not only logged
- guard against a transmission without enforcement

Login (auth.js)
- busy button; wrong credentials vs server unreachable vs server error

Asset ?v= versions bumped so browsers fetch the new files.
